\frac d{dx}\left((1-x^2)^2Q_n'\right)
 +(n-1)(n+2)(1-x^2)Q_n=0}.
$$
The boundary term vanishes at $x=\pm1$. Distinct eigenvalues are therefore orthogonal with weight $1-x^2$:
$$
\boxed{
\int_{-1}^{1}(1-x^2)Q_n(x)Q_m(x),dx=0,
\qquad n\ne m.}
$$

